			(property "Description" "6-pin header connection for use with the \"FTDI BASIC\" pinout - CABLE SIDE.\n\nAlso known as \"Arduino Serial Program Header\".\n\nThis is used on a design to provide a 6-pin connection point for serial communication usually from a USB cable (D+/D-) to these headers (RX/TX). It also has the remaining pins necessary for programming in the Arduino evironment (DTR, GND, and sometimes VCC).\n\nNote, this device has \"CABLE\" in the name.  It is intended to be used on a design that usually lives on the end of your USB cable and prvides the converter chip (FTDI232 or FTDI231x) to commnicate serial RX/TX.\n\nThe \"sister\" device, named \"TARGET\" is inteneded to be used on a design that contains a target micro-controller that you wish to program.\n\nYou can populate with some of these:\n\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/115  Female Headers (PRT-00115)\n\nFor reference (or to suit your programming needs) check out these designs:\n\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/9716  SparkFun FTDI Basic Breakout - 5V (DEV-09716)\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/9873  SparkFun FTDI Basic Breakout - 3.3V (DEV-09873)\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/12935  SparkFun FTDI SmartBasic (DEV-12935)\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/13746  SparkFun Beefy 3 - FTDI Basic Breakout (DEV-13746)"
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
